WEBVTT

00:00:05.764 --> 00:00:12.177
Use a subreport when the same report block, such as a client header, belongs in several document layouts.

00:00:15.802 --> 00:00:22.397
The parent report defines an invoice, receipt or lab report. The child file holds the reusable header layout.

00:00:28.455 --> 00:00:32.242
Start a blank parent report and add a Subreport from Components.

00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:46.078
The child JSON is attached to the parent. Set the subreport width to 180 millimeters, matching this A4 page’s printable area, so both logos and the company details fit on one line.

00:00:50.554 --> 00:00:58.115
Switch to Code and see the child definition attached to the parent JSON. The selected report file travels with the rest of the layout.

00:01:03.376 --> 00:01:10.537
Preview the actual PDF to check the logo sources and alignment. Linked images need URLs the reporting server can reach.

00:01:20.809 --> 00:01:31.016
Start another blank parent and select the same source file to reuse it. The designer stores an attached snapshot in each parent; choose the updated file again when the source changes.

00:01:35.889 --> 00:01:43.072
A host application can keep child JSON in its shared report library and send the version it selected when it renders each parent.
